<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Church of Sainte-Foy, Sélestat</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">12th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Church of Sainte-Foy in Sélestat, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alsace">Alsace</a>, is a Romanesque church built in the 12th century for a priory dependent on the abbey of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/conques">Conques</a>. Built of red and yellow sandstone, with an octagonal crossing tower, it is one of the major Romanesque buildings of Alsace.</p></div>
